			"element": "EnumItem",
			"enum": "StreamingIntegrityMode",
			"item": "Default",
			"part": "description",
			"before": "Default behavior (currently no change to gameplay).",
			"after": "Default behavior (currently equivalent to <strong>Disabled</strong>).",
			"value": {
				"Name": "Default",
				"Value": 0
			}
		},
		{
			"element": "EnumItem",
			"enum": "StreamingIntegrityMode",
			"item": "Disabled",
			"part": "description",
			"before": "<strong>Pausing Behavior</strong> - When a locally-simulated mechanism is not in a streamed-in region, its simulation is paused, but simulation of other locally-owned mechanisms continues. The only exception is that simulation of the replication focus is never paused, even if it's outside of a streamed-in region.",
			"after": "Simulation of the replication focus is never paused, regardless of the amount of content streamed in on the client.",
			"value": {
				"Name": "Disabled",
				"Value": 1
			}
		},
		{
			"element": "EnumItem",
			"enum": "StreamingIntegrityMode",
			"item": "MinimumRadiusPause",
			"part": "description",
			"before": "<strong>Pausing Criteria</strong> - The client triggers a pause when it does <strong>not</strong> have content streamed in up to at least <code>Workspace.StreamingMinRadius</code>. <strong>Unpausing Criteria</strong> - The client unpauses when it has content loaded up to <code>Workspace.StreamingMinRadius</code>. If the player's character is moving at a high rate of speed when the pause begins, the client might wait longer to resume in order to avoid rapid pausing and unpausing. <strong>Pausing Behavior</strong> - When a pause is triggered, all local simulation on the client is paused and the <code>Player.GameplayPaused</code> property is set.",
			"after": "All client-side simulation is paused when content is not streamed in up to the minimum radius.",
			"value": {
				"Name": "MinimumRadiusPause",
				"Value": 2
			}
		},
		{
			"element": "EnumItem",
			"enum": "StreamingIntegrityMode",
			"item": "PauseOutsideLoadedArea",
			"part": "description",
			"before": "<strong>Pausing Criteria</strong> - The client triggers a pause when the replication focus is not in a streamed-in region. <strong>Unpausing Criteria</strong> - The client unpauses when the replication focus is inside a streamed-in region. Similar to <strong>MinimumRadiusPause</strong>, the client might wait longer to resume if the player's character is moving at a high rate of speed. <strong>Pausing Behavior</strong> - Similar to <strong>Disabled</strong> but no exception for the replication focus. If simulation of the replication focus is paused, the <code>Player.GameplayPaused</code> property is set.",
			"after": "Simulation of the replication focus is paused when any part of its bounding box is not in a streamed-in area.",
			"value": {
				"Name": "PauseOutsideLoadedArea",
				"Value": 3
			}
		}
